config VS_VOICE_PROMPT_MAX_BYTES
	int "VelaSight idle assistant prompt budget (bytes)"
	default 32768
	range 2048 131072
	depends on LVX_USE_DEMO_CONTEST2026_264_VELASIGHT

config VS_VOICE_TRANSCRIPT_MAX_BYTES
	int "VelaSight idle assistant social transcript budget (bytes)"
	default 4096
	range 0 32768
	depends on LVX_USE_DEMO_CONTEST2026_264_VELASIGHT
	---help---
		How much of a social record's spoken transcript is put in front of
		the model, as its own message alongside the record reference.

		The transcript is audioTimeline from the end-of-session minutes:
		one entry per recognised sentence, each with its own timestamps and
		emotion.  It is the only place the words of a conversation exist --
		txtMinutes is a summary of it, not a copy -- so without this the
		assistant can answer "how did it go" but not "what did he say".

		Sized against what a session produces rather than what the prompt
		could hold.  Rendered one line per sentence and stripped of the
		fields the model has no use for, a sentence costs roughly 30 bytes
		against the 164 its JSON does, so 4096 carries something like 130
		sentences -- about ten minutes of conversation at the density of
		the sample records.  A longer session is truncated with a line
		saying how many sentences were dropped, so the model is never left
		to assume it saw everything.

		Raising this spends prompt budget, which
		CONFIG_VS_VOICE_PROMPT_MAX_BYTES bounds and the context compactor
		competes for.  Zero disables the transcript entirely and restores
		the previous behaviour of sending only the summary.

config VS_VOICE_RESP_MAX_BYTES
	int "VelaSight idle assistant model response buffer (bytes)"
	default 32768
	range 8192 131072
	depends on LVX_USE_DEMO_CONTEST2026_264_VELASIGHT

config VS_VOICE_RECORD_MAX_MS
	int "VelaSight idle assistant listening window (ms)"
	default 15000
	range 3000 60000
	depends on LVX_USE_DEMO_CONTEST2026_264_VELASIGHT
	---help---
		How long one utterance is recorded when the user does not end it
		with the confirm key.

		This is the only thing that ends an utterance automatically.  The
		assistant deliberately has no local speech detector: an energy
		threshold calibrated for a different microphone sat above normal
		speech at this board's gain and silently discarded whole
		recordings, so ending a round is left to the confirm key, the back
		key, and the recognizer's own verdict on whether there was
		anything to transcribe.

		It therefore serves two purposes: a bound on how long a user who
		walked away is listened to before the conversation is written to
		chat history, and a safety net if a key event is ever missed.
		Because a truncated question is worse than a short wait, prefer
		raising this over lowering it.

config VS_VOICE_STACKSIZE
	int "VelaSight idle assistant worker thread stack (bytes)"
	default 16384
	range 8192 32768
	depends on LVX_USE_DEMO_CONTEST2026_264_VELASIGHT

